#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# elliptic_f

#% text
# `elliptic_f(phi, m)` gives the incomplete elliptic integral of the first kind `F(phi | m)`, the integral of `1/sqrt(1 - m*sin(t)^2)` for `t` from 0 to `phi`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 19.2.4 with `k^2 = m`. `F(pi/2 | m)` is `elliptic_k(m)`, and `F(phi | 0)` is `phi`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values. `elliptic_f` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
elliptic_f(pi/4, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.8260178762492452

#% cell
elliptic_f(1.0, 0)
#% output
#= 1.0

#% cell
elliptic_f(pi/2, 0.5) - elliptic_k(0.5)
#% output
#= 2.220446049250313e-16

#% cell
n(elliptic_f(1, 1/3), 30)
#% output
#= 1.0515224356380810195409081596619524

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `jacobi_amplitude` inverts it in `phi`:

#% cell
jacobi_amplitude(elliptic_f(0.8, 0.3), 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.8

#% text
# The derivative in `phi`:

#% cell
d(elliptic_f(phi, m), phi)
#% output
#= (1 - m*sin(phi)^2)^(-1/2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `elliptic_k`, `elliptic_e`, `jacobi_amplitude`, `inverse_jacobi_sn`
